65	### 0.3 Campaign state machine (`internal/campaign`, rule 7)
66	- **Transition table**:
67	  - draft→generating;
68	  - generating→in_review | generation_failed | cancelled;
69	  - generation_failed→generating | cancelled;
70	  - in_review→in_review (edit) | generating (regenerate) | approved | rejected | cancelled;
71	  - approved→sending | cancelled;
72	  - sending→completed | completed_with_failures | cancelled.
73	- **Guarded update**: `UPDATE campaigns SET state=$to, version=version+1 WHERE id=$1 AND state=$from AND version=$v`. Zero rows means `ErrConflict` (409). Every transition writes a `campaign_events` row.
74	- **Create**: the brief is 1 to 2,000 characters. `campaign_url` must be https, on a host in `CAMPAIGN_URL_HOSTS`, and at most 40 characters.
75	- **Edit**: `ValidateRevision` runs the revision schema, then the segment and content validators, with paths prefixed `/segment` and `/content`. A human edit becomes a new revision (`source=human`); its audience is recounted and the state stays `in_review`. An invalid edit gets a 422 and is never stored.
76	- **API**:
77	  - `POST /api/campaigns`;
78	  - `GET /api/campaigns/{id}` (campaign, latest revision, audit trail);
79	  - `POST /api/campaigns/{id}/revisions` (takes `base_revision_id` and `version`);
80	  - `/reject` and `/cancel`.
81	
82	  Approve arrives in stage B, together with fan-out.
83	- **Tests**:
84	  - the full from×to matrix, where every pair not in the table is rejected;
85	  - a stale version gives 409;
86	  - two concurrent transitions: exactly one wins;
87	  - audit rows are written;
88	  - an invalid human edit gets 422 and leaves no revision.
